The advanced Entity operations controls are for manual native operations. Normal blueprint capture and placement do not require users to enter UUIDs or runtime handles.

== Undo, errors, and recovery ==

Undo checks target voxels and props before restoring the saved snapshot. It pauses if cells changed after placement. It also checks the live handle and transform of each placed prop before removing it. If a native operation fails, the mod attempts to restore its pre-paste snapshot. If the result cannot be verified, it keeps recovery state for another undo attempt.

If a server operation stops reporting progress for 10 seconds, the client marks it as potentially stuck and offers Reset / release. The client keeps paste locked until the server confirms it discarded the operation's recovery journal and released its lock. Releasing an operation may leave partial terrain or props behind, and the abandoned operation can no longer be undone. If confirmation is lost, request release again. An unreachable server leaves paste paused until release is confirmed.

Progress and operation results are written to the role-appropriate ShroudForge log under the <code>world-editor</code> source. The editor has no separate UI log. A successful live readback confirms the in-world result. It does not prove that the game save persists after reload.

